All six phases are implemented and verified. Summary of what shipped:

Data plane — migrations/2026-07-25_pm-mobile-relay.sql (+ schema.sql): pm_live / pm_commands tables, flat RLS (no EXISTS subqueries), Realtime enabled.

Laptop bridge — scripts/pm/bridge.mjs, started via pnpm pm --bridge. Outbound-only: publishes checklist tasks (~40–80KB, not 7MB), delivery session state, and a fleet rollup; drains phone commands through the same routeDelivery() the desktop UI uses. Split into two Supabase-free pure cores (createCommandExecutor, createTasksSnapshotBuilder) for testability.

Push — src/app/api/pm/notify/route.ts, the first-ever consumer of the notification.requested event that's been emitted and discarded since DLV-1.

Mobile UI — /pm/live: Checklist tab (tick round-trips to the real .md), Delivery tab (pause/abort/resume/cancel, gate-aware cards, inline Q&A), Launch flow (mandatory envelope, refuses on dirty/red), Usage tab, bridge-liveness chip.

Tests — tests/pm-bridge.test.ts, 12/12 passing: allowlist enforcement, gate-approval refusal, launch guardrails, tick drift detection, payload-size budget.

Docs — PM Dashboard Refactor and Delivery 10x checklists/feature-state updated (DLV-20/21/22, R29), and a full amendment recorded in Delivery 10x/6 - Design Debates & Rejected Ideas.md explaining why this doesn't reopen the "remote decision controls" rejection — plus a new Atlas entry.

Verification: pnpm pm:lint 0 errors, pnpm typecheck/pnpm test show zero regressions against the pre-existing baseline, pnpm build succeeds with both new routes compiled, pnpm docs:check passes.

